    "updated_at": "2022-06-07T17:00:15Z",
    "body": "I don't think the EBNF allows for the second code point to be U+0001 when the first is `:`, for instance. At least the intent was to prevent that. Does EBNF work completely differently from ABNF in that `|` doesn't signify OR but instead \"union\"?\r\n\r\n(I didn't see \"An equivalent EBNF is the following\" initially and I don't think what it states is correct.)",
