    "updated_at": "2022-06-07T17:28:29Z",
    "body": "I think that is done. The other way I could write this is by looping over the characters individually, which is what a performant implementation would do (instead of using lots of O(n) \"contains\" operations). But I think this is relatively clear.\r\n\r\n(Edit: well, a performant implementation would be looping over code _units_, since that's JS's native string format... which feels ickier to spec.)",
