    "created_at": "2025-05-23T00:06:02Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-05-23T00:06:02Z",
    "body": "> The first character needs to be ASCII alpha. But `<x<script>` would have tagname `x<script`, which matches the HTML parser.\r\n\r\nRight, ok. And I guess the important part is that if this is already allowed by the parser, then whatever problems this does cause must have already been handled. Or they're not problems.\r\n\r\nThanks.",
