    "body": "> Right, ok. And I guess the important part is that if this is already allowed by the parser, then whatever problems this does cause must have already been handled. Or they're not problems.\r\n\r\nThis is the main reason I'm not worried.\r\n\r\nRegarding your question about history, I traced back through a variety of bugs; https://issues.chromium.org/issues/41276288#comment20 is one of the older nodes in the graph. I don't think `<` ever came up specifically though.",
